we've been recently contacted by a  source that has insider information  with what apple is doing with their  higher end apple silicon max  including both the high-end imac and the  mac pro  and based on what this source has told  us we can finally put a ton of puzzle  pieces together  including some recent leaks and reports  from reputable sources  like mark german to nail down both the  release date  and various specs and features of the  high-end imac  so let's get right into it the main  piece of info our source gave us is that  there will not be  an imac pro or a very expensive imac  the source said that apple is  constraining how far they take the imac  based on a 2 000 retail consumer price  target  which is similar to the current 27-inch  imax price  the reason for that is that apple wants  to be more consumer-focused for their  apple silicon max  lowering the prices compared to how  expensive the old intel models could be  configured  the main reason is that when it comes to  the mac most people buy the lower end  max  since they're much easier to afford a  smaller percentage would go for the 16  inch macbook pro  and 27 inch imac and an even smaller  percentage  would go for the intel based imac pro  and then an  even smaller percentage of people would  spec them out  with the highest end intel chips so the  source is basically saying that the now  discontinued imac pro  is dead with no more refresh expected to  come  and if you think about it the m1 max  have basically proven to apple  and the world that going for lower entry  level prices  with apple silicon was enough to cause  max sales to absolutely skyrocket  and break records in terms of sales even  though  all of those new macs share just a  single  m1 chat so because of that successful  strategy  the mac lineup including the high-end  imac will now be more consumer focused  and the source says that the new smaller  apple silicon mac pro  will basically be there as the high-end  customizable option for the heavy  professionals out there  and interestingly the source claims that  even the mac pro will see  a huge price decrease starting somewhere  at around  3 000 plus dollars at the base price  which is half the price of the current  intel mac pro  and it's all due to apple saving tons of  cash by using their own  apple design chips instead of paying  intel for cpus  and amd for discrete gpus that right  there is also another reason why the  imac pro  isn't coming back there just isn't  enough of a gap  between the 2 000 imac and the 3 000  mac pro to warrant an imac pro to fit in  between  those price points now moving on i fully  believe that the high-end imac will for  sure  have a chin just like the 24 inch imac  for a few different reasons first off  the larger imac has  always looked exactly like the lower end  models in the past  so it makes total sense for the upcoming  larger imac  to match the 24 inch imac in terms of  the design  which will allow apple to use these  side-by-side marketing images  of both imac sizes now don't worry the  chin  doesn't necessarily mean that it's going  to look bad because  even if the chin is the same height as  on the 24 inch imac  the larger display size on the high-end  version will actually make it look  much slimmer on the larger imac display  as you can see in this image that i drew  up in photoshop and on top of that i can  also guarantee that apple will be able  to fit the entire logic  board into the chin area just like  they're already doing with the 24 inch  imac  because increasing the display size will  allow them to increase  the thickness of the mac itself by  around 25 percent  to help fit a thicker logic board all  while keeping the relative dimensions  looking proper and balanced compared to  the 24  inch model and if you think about it a  larger display would mean that the chin  itself  would become significantly longer giving  apple even more room  for a longer logic board so based on all  of that  it honestly really just makes sense to  keep the chin around  on the high-end imac to keep the design  language the same  between both sizes since apple has  always done that in the past  and for that same reason i can basically  guarantee that the larger imac will have  white bezels just like the current 24  inch model  the main reason is that many buyers of  the 24 inch imac  have been pleasantly surprised by how  well the white bezels blend  into light or white colored walls  actually being much less distracting  than the current black bezels and then  if you add in the fact that the bezels  will look even slimmer  and less noticeable on the high-end imac  because of the larger display  it makes total sense for the bezels to  be white and now before i get into the  interesting details about the apple  silicon chip specs and release date  i want to get into the actual display  size of the imac  itself i can 100 guarantee that the imac  will not  have a 32 inch display because that  would make the imac  larger than the 32 inch pro display xdr  which makes no sense at all on top of  that our source says that the cost of  taking the imac  to a 30 inch or larger display would  push the price  beyond apple's 2 000 retail price target  for the imac  so it needs to stay under 30 inches my  source also believes that apple is  working on a cheaper  external display which will not use many  led technology like the pro display xdr  with a price target of around twelve  hundred dollars  and if you didn't already know this  apple's 27 inch imac  uses the same exact panel as lg's  ultrafine  5k display that apple sells on their  website  so i expect the new display panel that  apple is working on  to be identical to the one that's going  into the higher end imac  and because of all this i'd have to  place my bets that the new high-end imac  will have either a 28 inch display or a  29.5 inch display which apple would mark  it as a 30  inch now moving on to the chip situation  i'm now  100 sure that the high-end imac will be  getting  the m1x chip as the only chip option  for a few different reasons first off  the twitter user dylan dkt  has recently confirmed that the high-end  imac will be released next year  and in mark german's recent edition of  his newsletter  he basically agreed to the exact same  thing this totally makes sense because  if you think about it  apple revealed the m1 imac five months  after revealing the  m1 macbooks and it ended up getting the  exact  same channel so apple could end up doing  the same exact thing for the high-end  imac  giving it the same m1x chip that we're  expecting for the 14  and 16 inch macbook pros the second  reason is that dylan believes  that the m1x chip will be going into the  higher end mac mini  the 14 and 16 inch macbook pros and the  higher end imac  which i totally agree with now mark  german says that there's  a chance that it'll be getting the m2x  chip instead  but i don't think so because apple would  be skipping a generation  which is wasted potential because giving  this imac the m1x  will provide a much easier upgrade path  for the next imac refresh  while at the same time keeping the  entire current mac lineup  in line with the same m1 based ip  now on top of that dylan also confirmed  that upcoming apple silicon max  will not feature any kind of discrete  gpu on mac  other than the mac pro so this points to  the imac getting the m1x chip  as the only chip option but of course  apple will likely utilize chip binning  to lower the base price and give users  some upgrade options  similar to what they did with the 24  inch imac except this time around  i expect apple to offer either a 12 core  16 core  or 32 core gpu now finally getting to  the release date  dillon explained that the imac has been  delayed until next year  with the main reason being that apple  doesn't want their devices  to compete for attention and delays in  product releases  have led to this timetable what he means  is that we were initially expecting the  14  and 16 inch m1x macbook pros to come at  wwdc  in june and in that case the imac would  have been released in the fall  but since the macbooks got pushed back  apple is  also pushing back the imac just to  spread out the timetable of releases  because if apple released the m1x  macbook pros mac mini and  imac all at the same time the imac would  be  buried underneath the hype of the  macbook pros because they're obviously  much more popular  due to being portable laptops so apple  is simply going to delay the imac for a  few months  even if they have to sit on a shelf  somewhere just so that the imac can  shine in its own spotlight and this is  even more evidence  that it's packing an m1x chip instead of  a future m2x  now to give you even more evidence mark  german's power on newsletter  shows that apple will just barely hit  their two-year apple silicon transition  target  with the 2022 apple silicon mac pro  getting released at the end of next year  in november  so because of that apple likely doesn't  want to release the larger imac at the  same time as the mac pro  since they'll be competing for attention  so in reality  it kind of has to get released in the  first half of next year  and if we go even further both mark  german and dylan  agree that a redesigned macbook air is  coming next year  with dylan claiming that it's going to  come in the first half  of 2022 with a brand new m2 chip  which i totally agree with and i fully  believe that this new m2 chip  deserves its own apple event and that's  why i'm personally predicting  that the macbook air will be revealed in  march and because of that  i think it makes total sense for the m1x  high-end imac to be released before  that event happens potentially through a  simple press release  since apple has already showed off the  new redesign with the 24 inch imac  and now finally let's finish off with  the pricing  our source believes that the base model  will remain at  or under two thousand dollars which  makes total sense  and in my opinion the price of the imac  fully depends on the price of the  upcoming 14 inch macbook pro  if the 14 inch sticks to the same 1799  dollar price tag then the imac will  match it  but if the 14 inch goes up to 19.99  then the imac will also be priced at  19.99  guaranteed but no more than two thousand  dollars for the base price  for sure so with all that said here's my  full prediction list for the features  and specs  which is definitely subject to change as  more and more leaks and rumors get  released  but for now i'm pretty confident in all  of these details  now if you totally disagree with me then  let me know your thoughts down in the  comment section below  but if you enjoyed this video go ahead  and click the circle above to subscribe  for more videos like this one definitely  check out one of those two right over  there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video

